/// A top-level function may be overloaded.
///
/// Methods already overload, in both processors, and the emitter already
/// mangles a method's signature into its symbol -- m_P_Show_1_Integer beside
/// m_P_Show_1_String.  So the machinery exists and only file scope refuses it,
/// with ''Show'' is already defined.'
///
/// ⚠️ That asymmetry is the whole argument for this: the same two declarations
/// are legal inside a class and illegal outside one, which is a place the
/// language stopped rather than a decision it made.
///
/// Fails with: 'Show' is already defined.  (file rejected -- no test ran)
///
function Show (N : Integer) : String;
begin
    Exit 'int';
end

function Show (S : String) : String;
begin
    Exit 'str';
end

test 'A top-level function may be overloaded';
begin
    AssertEqual ('int', Show (1));
    AssertEqual ('str', Show (Str ('a')));
end
